how do you find the mentor so I got a  great question for my youtube viewers  Tom love you guys who wrote in to say  how do you find the mentor this is a  great question and one that a lot of  entrepreneurs a ski you know you realize  you can't do everything yourself and you  don't need to come up with every single  new idea yourself if you have somebody  who has already done it and leverage  what they've learned to help you grow  its way faster to achieve your goal than  to try to figure it all out yourself in  my mind there are two types of mentors  and you can leverage both to help you  grow your business the first people are  what I call aspirational mentors they're  people who you never meet but can still  give you lots of great advice so my  first aspirational mentor was Bill Gates  I had a software company Bill Gates was  the biggest guy in software I never met  bill gates the Bill Gates saved my  company okay I was gonna quit I was I  told my business partner that I quit I  was in tears I thought of giving up I  thought I had tried everything and I  started researching Bill Gates I realize  you know what I'm not the first guy to  try to sell software and I research Bill  Gates in his story and how he started  Microsoft and how he built his business  up and a lot of it was through  partnerships and so I applied that same  strategy apart of my business and within  a couple months i got my first deal the  first year was 13 and a half thousand  dollars and not that like that saved my  business i was making 300 bucks a month  and here was a 13 and a half thousand  dollar order it was amazing i mean i  seem like a lot to you guys now but that  that changed my life and then I was able  to close another deal on another deal  another deal and that was all because of  Bill Gates and I had never met him I  just researched his story I now I look  up to AP Giannini who is a founder bank  of america and steve jobs to the front  of apple and these guys teach me things  AP patines AP Giannini he's been dead  for years and Steve Jobs I'll you know  recently passed away I've never met  these people but they're impacting my  business and I consider them my mentors  so what  but you're trying to do find someone  who's already done it and research their  success the bigger they are the easier  it is to find out what their story is so  the second kind of mentor is actually  somebody you can talk to write some you  can go have a coffee with and bounce  ideas off of the challenge for a lot of  entrepreneurs is they go up to people  and say hey will you be my mentor and  right away you freak people out you know  it's like asking somebody off the street  will you marry me it doesn't happen  mentorship is a relationship you have to  get to know each other you have to work  well together you have to have trust you  have to build that up it's not something  you just jump into so if you want  somebody to mentor you don't don't email  them and say will you be my mentor  because it's too much of an ask the  better thing to do is connect with  somebody and ask them for for 20 minutes  of their time awesome for a phone call  for a coffee show your interest because  people like helping other people if you  have a passion and you seem really  excited and interested in learning then  people will want to help you out mentors  gain as well we feel good giving advice  to mentees if if we feel like that  person is actually going to go and do  something with it right they're going to  take that knowledge and apply it and if  I get that for people who write to me if  I get that sense of excitement and  passion and and willingness to follow  through that I'm happy to help them out  but it starts by building a relationship  so 20 minutes over coffee I remember I  had one person right into means and say  I want to meet with you even if it's  walking with you on the way to a meeting  let me know I'll bring you some cookies  and we'll chat on the walk right that  shows drive and determination and so let  that come out when you're approaching  people and have a simple ask and after  that 20 minutes if your passion comes  through and they are feeling your vibe  and feel like you're taking their advice  it's usually pretty easy to say hey  would you mind if I if I called you back  in a month if I had more questions going  to reach out to you almost everybody's  going to say yes unless your total  douche bag you know in the meeting and  super early because you're not  respecting their time  then they're going to say yes and that  starts the relationship and it can build  to something more right but you got to  start it off small and simple and easy  make it easy for people to say yes and  not throw this huge commitment in front  of them so if you know somebody who  you're trying to target right that you  know there's somebody you have in mind  who's this big shot or whoever it is  then you can reach out to them with  something simple like that and let your  passion shine through and in one of my  mizuka guides on finding a mentor I have  a script that you can use as an email  template to connect with people if you  don't know who you want to connect with  you don't have an idea of the person  that you want to go to then start  reaching out to your network ID let them  know who you're looking for the first  mentor that I had the real mentor was a  guy by the name of John and I found  jamba going to my bank because I I had  no connections I was 19 I had no  connections you know I didn't want to  ask my parents I wanted to you know feel  like I'm doing this myself and not being  supported because you know my mom's  friend is helping me and I had no  personal connections my friends are all  in school right so I went to the bank I  thought the bank is gonna be a friend of  entrepreneurs that's obviously not what  the bank does is giving advice but they  connected me with somebody named Michael  who i thought you know great Michael  this guy's got this downtown office and  you know nice views of the city and  looks like a really big big guy a big  shot and he was just all air he was all  air but he introduced us to another guy  named Steve who tried to help us out but  couldn't and he introduced us to another  friend named John and John ended up  being an awesome force for our company  and taught us and trained us and gave us  lots of advice and ended up helping us  sell our business and so such a strange  paths but that's how it builds right I  spoke to my bank I had no contact say I  just walked into my bank and then they  put me on the somebody put me on to  somebody and get put me on to John and  and it may happen faster for you but  it's put in that message out there to  your contacts to your network or the  type of person you're looking for and  setting up times to go meet people  so that's my advice find your aspiration  lament or find someone who's done what  you're trying to do and research how  they got started and then for an actual  you know in person human that you can  talk to make it simple easy low-risk 20  minutes over coffee show your passion  let that shine through and if you don't  know anybody yet to go after start  putting out to your connections your  network or the type of person you're  looking for and the venture will come if  you have persistence that's how you find  a mentor believe for those are watching  I love to hear in the comments leave a  comment as to how you found your mentor  how you looking for a mentor who your  mentors are I love to hear from you in  the comments below if you like these  videos you can click on the link to  support me in the description and click  on my face here to subscribe to the  channel thank you so much I'll see you  soon
 

